{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Of old</b> — the meaning of \"Your years\" — \"for ever.\" Only that there is no force in the word רק in the manner of human speech." "And the meaning of <b>of old</b> — for You are prior to the earth that You founded. And the meaning that is poured out for the heaven of heavens is in complete proofs." "<b>And the heavens are the work of Your hands</b> — for it is the horizontal line." "<b>And the heavens are the work of Your hands</b> — it is the firmament, and they endure in their universals and perish in their particulars. Therefore he says: \"They shall perish,\" for the particulars perish and the universals are preserved. And this is what he says, \"for the heavens shall vanish like smoke and the earth shall wear out like a garment\" — regarding the particulars he said it, those that go out from the universal, for they change and perish; only the universals, which are the laws, He established as a statute that shall not pass, and the earth endures forever."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 102, :notes {3 "The reading היוצאים מן הכלל (those that go out from the universal) is translated hyper-literally; the syntactic relationship of this subordinate phrase to what precedes is unclear in the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:56.343306590Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}